# Example alerting config for the monthly SJR refresh (Termux).
# Copy to ~/.sjr_refresh.env (kept OUTSIDE the repo so secrets aren't committed)
# and source it before running the refresh, e.g. in your scheduler entry:
#   set -a; . "$HOME/.sjr_refresh.env"; set +a; bash scripts/termux_refresh_sjr.sh
# (termux_run_refresh.sh already does this if the file exists.)

# --- Dead-man's switch (healthchecks.io) ---
# Create a check at https://healthchecks.io, set its period to ~35 days, and
# paste its ping URL here. The script pings <URL>/start, <URL> on success, and
# <URL>/fail on failure; healthchecks emails you if a run is ever missed.
# HEALTHCHECKS_URL=https://hc-ping.com/your-uuid-here

# --- Telegram status messages ---
# Create a bot via @BotFather to get the token, and get your chat id from
# @userinfobot. Both must be set to receive success/failure messages.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123456789:ABCdefGhIJKlmNoPQRstuVWxyz
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=123456789
